WEBVTT

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:51.750
Who knew the sun would shine so bright?
I had no idea.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:54.550
Being alive…

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:57.420
It feels amazing!

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:05.140
Damn it!

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:17.720
So you, too, were a participant in another game.

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:20.310
What are you here for?

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:22.910
What is it that you know?

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:25.230
I'm sorry, but I am not inclined to answer.

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:27.830
Althought, I could leave you with a clue.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:32.100
In this world, the radio still exists.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.020
I recommend looking into the ones in taxis.

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:38.270
Radio?

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:41.450
Everybody, listen up!

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:43.490
We have the answer!

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:47.300
Come to the beach, I repeat, the beach!

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.810
Beach?

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.790
Shibuki…

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:52.850
I'm worried…

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:54.870
I'm scared…

00:01:54.870 --> 00:02:01.200
When tomorrow comes,
I'll have to participate in these games again…

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:04.030
But I'm… I'm…

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:06.780
not as strong as the rest of you.

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:13.170
I'm trembling, aren't I?

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.460
I feel the same way as you.

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:19.050
I didn't take part in the last game…

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:21.240
Because I was afraid…

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:22.930
I am afraid.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:26.790
I'm also different from the other two…

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.270
I'm scared.

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:29.720
I'm so scared!

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:32.190
I want to go back…

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:35.140
I want to go back to my world.

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:39.320
I don't care if I go back to being bored.

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:41.290
Because of that…

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:43.070
I want to return…

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:57.840
Thanks.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:59.150
Um…

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:01.010
I'm Usagi.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.180
Usagi Yuzuha.

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:05.190
Um, Usagi…

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:09.110
We can survive together.
Will you come with us?

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:10.900
I'm sorry, but…

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:13.100
I'm better off by myself.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:17.560
I won't survive if I get too close
and give in to my feelings.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.020
Feelings?

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:20.960
When you get together to survive the game,

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:25.860
the day may come when they have to kill you.

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:30.240
That can't happen.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:35.460
I'll… survive with all the others.

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:38.270
At the very least, now…

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:41.000
Let's make ourselves feel better.

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:54.700
The first game I participated in was Two of Hearts.

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.240
Heart?

00:03:56.240 --> 00:03:58.540
Games of Heart are psychology related.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:01.970
They destroy the minds of whoever
want to survive.

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:03.480
It's the worst kind of game.

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:08.290
Out of the four carriages,
one was filled with a lethal poison gas.

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:12.300
I had to use a gas mask
with three gas cylinders of oxygen to survive.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:14.150
So…

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:15.310
Yes…

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:18.020
I was short one gas mask.

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:22.230
I had to put it all on luck with the four carriages.

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:23.560
It was the worst…

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:28.290
Knowing you would die, you had to open the door.

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:32.000
But there isn't anyone in the world who would risk their life early into the game,

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:35.470
when they can feel so secure.

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:38.120
But you've survived that!

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:41.050
So you're a strong person after all.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:42.370
Not at all.

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:44.540
I was only terrified.

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:46.840
I gave up on thinking…

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:48.610
and opened the door.

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:54.660
I opened the door, waiting to die…

00:04:56.050 --> 00:04:57.580
Why?

00:05:00.350 --> 00:05:02.540
Why did I survive?

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:06.970
I've already died once before…

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:10.600
Because I was too weak of a human being.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:13.920
I'm only allowing myself to live for the moment.

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:17.930
It was an evil game that had you feel the absolute worst.

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:22.480
I'm happy to see you've survived for so long.

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:28.440
We both still have Alice…

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:30.400
and Karube.

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:41.190
I want to show everyone…

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:45.630
